    [Doc][3/N] Document GLM KDA RecoverSSM usage (#20134)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Document experimental GLM KDA RecoverSSM usage on Ascend Model Runner
    V2, split from #19133 as part 3/N. Include the serving options, A3/A5
    scope, cache and parallelism restrictions, eager/graph modes, Mooncake
    PD requirements and the experimental numerical behavior.
    
    This documentation accompanies the operators in [1/N,
    #20128](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/pull/20128) and
    framework integration in [2/N,
    #20131](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/pull/20131).
    
    Upstream references: [vLLM serving CLI
    (`--use-replayssm`)](https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/cli/serve/) and
    [CacheConfig
    API](https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/api/vllm/config/cache/). The
    upstream option documents Mamba2 ReplaySSM and defaults to disabled;
    this guide describes its reuse for Ascend GLM KDA RecoverSSM.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Documentation only. Add the user guide and release note for the combined
    RecoverSSM feature. The guide is extracted from #19133 with upstream
    ReplaySSM reference links; the release note is associated with this
    documentation PR.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    1. Compared the extracted guide with #19133 and checked its options and
    restrictions against the framework configuration validation.
    2. Checked Markdown formatting, spelling, whitespace and the
    release-note YAML structure.
    3. For the reference update, verified the upstream CLI and CacheConfig
    pages; Markdownlint, Codespell and `git diff --check` passed. Full `bash
    format.sh ci` was attempted, but actionlint environment installation
    timed out after 300 seconds.
    
    The integrated-model test results for the operator/framework combination
    are recorded in #20131.
    
